{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SEAM ANALYSIS COMPLETE — a decided split, with the test-seam risk checked per member. This resolves\nthis ticket's Approach from \"candidate\" to a concrete plan.\n\nRECOMMENDED ORDER, and why this order:\n\n1) gate_dispatch.py (799) -> extract the PLAN-REVIEW RECOVERY cluster into a new\n   src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py (~300 LOC). gate_dispatch lands at ~518.\n   Members: the STEP_* constants + _PLAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED_STEP_IDS (:51-68), GateContractError\n   (:71-75), _collect_step_ids (:78-91), _validate_gate_step_ids (:94-108), _DET_STEP_IDS/\n   _LLM_STEP_KINDS (:243-246), _attach_plan_review_metrics (:249-334),\n   _recover_plan_review_coach_failure (:337-380), _recover_plan_review_verify_failure (:383-444),\n   _degraded_plan_review_verdict (:447-480).\n   The cluster is REAL, not carved: _validate_gate_step_ids calls _collect_step_ids; all three\n   reconstruction functions key off the STEP_* ids; the file's own comment at :51-57 says the\n   constants exist FOR the recovery/metrics logic. Only produce_plan_review_verdict calls in, and\n   only at the cluster's top edge — no mid-cluster entry.\n   WHY FIRST: it is the only candidate with ZERO string-monkeypatched members, AND it carries all\n   THREE of gate_dispatch's five finalize_verdict call sites (:377, :441, :478) into a module with\n   ~500 lines of headroom — which is precisely what unblocks 343b's gap-5 wiring.\n\n2) orchestrator.py (796) -> extract the run-scoped CONTEXT-ASSEMBLY cluster (:88-244, ~157 LOC) into\n   src/rebar/llm/plan_review/context_assembly.py. orchestrator lands at ~641, leaving finalize_verdict\n   in place with ~160 lines of room for 343b's parameter.\n   Members: _assemble_cache, assemble_context_cache, _assemble_cache_key, assemble_context,\n   _assemble_context_uncached. One purpose: read the ticket graph once per gate run and memoize it.\n\n3) DO NOT extract the code-review gate cluster (:481-729) in this ticket. code_review_enabled is\n   monkeypatched BY STRING on the gate_dispatch module object at 14 sites, and its sole internal\n   caller _code_review_preflight would move with it — so the moved caller would read the NEW module's\n   binding and all 14 patches would silently stop taking effect. Making it work requires converting\n   that reference to a module-attribute lookup, which is a DESIGN CHANGE, not a relocation, and must\n   not be smuggled into a size-driven split. Separate ticket.\n\nZERO-TEST-EDIT MECHANISM (the 2682/3a98 precedent): re-import the moved names back into the origin\nmodule so they remain ITS module-globals. Verified for every Seam-B member — all external references\nare either `from ... import X` or `gate_dispatch.X` attribute access, both of which survive a\nre-import. Includes pytest.raises(gate_dispatch.GateContractError), which holds because it is the\nsame class object.\n\nTWO LOAD-BEARING CAUTIONS FOUND IN THE ANALYSIS:\n- PRESERVE THE REFERENCE STYLE. The recovery functions reach orchestrator via a lazy\n  `from rebar.llm.plan_review import orchestrator` then ATTRIBUTE access (orchestrator.finalize_verdict\n  etc.). tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_execution_floor_lifecycle.py:85 monkeypatches\n  orchestrator.pass3_over_findings and then calls the recovery function. Flattening to\n  `from ...orchestrator import pass3_over_findings` would silently break that patch. Move the code\n  VERBATIM.\n- MOVE THE STEP_* CONSTANTS WITH THE CLUSTER rather than leaving them behind. Leaving them creates a\n  genuine module-level cycle; the alternative (mirroring the strings locally, as\n  code_review/finalize.py:22-27 already does) would create a THIRD copy of those strings, and\n  finalize.py:14-15 already carries a \"must be mirrored\" warning. Single source of truth is both\n  safer and cheaper here.\n\nIMPORT-CYCLE CHECKS (both clean, no TYPE_CHECKING guard needed):\n- plan_review_recovery.py needs only `from __future__ import annotations` + typing.Any at module\n  level; every other import is already lazy inside the moved bodies. One-way edge\n  gate_dispatch -> plan_review_recovery, mirroring code_review/finalize.py's posture.\n- context_assembly.py imports only siblings/leaves (det_floor, sizing, config), none of which import\n  orchestrator. NOTE production_batch_runner.py:49 does `from .orchestrator import assemble_context,\n  route_criteria`, so the re-import into orchestrator is LOAD-BEARING, not cosmetic."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785466579309988001,"uuid":"5d058cd6-8b12-4226-aa8d-2b97ccf800a3"}